Fix: KV LOAD/STORE/EVICT lines (v1/kv_offload/transfer_log.py,
VLLM_KV_TRANSFER_LOG) and the periodic "KV Transfer metrics: ..." line
(distributed/kv_transfer/kv_connector/v1/metrics.py,
VLLM_KV_TRANSFER_METRICS_LOG) were both on by default -- too much detail
for routine watching even after readability fixes, per direct feedback
listing five example lines still cluttering the default log (RAM->fs
cascade legs, VRAM->RAM store lines, EVICT lines, and the raw metrics
dump).

Both switches already existed (this session, kv-transfer-log-clarity.patch
/ kv-transfer-evict-log.patch / kv-transfer-metrics-log-readability.patch)
-- this is purely a default flip, no new flag introduced: "1" -> "0" for
VLLM_KV_TRANSFER_LOG (which already gates all of LOAD, STORE, and EVICT
-- one switch, not three), and "1" -> "0" for
VLLM_KV_TRANSFER_METRICS_LOG. Set either to 1 to watch that detail live.
Neither change touches v1/engine/request_lifecycle_log.py's NEW
REQUEST/FINISHED lines (VLLM_REQUEST_LIFECYCLE_LOG, still on by
default) -- those are the per-request summary meant to be the everyday
default view; this patch demotes only the per-transfer/per-metric detail
one tier below it, matching the same "default quiet, opt into more"
shape as the ITERATION_LOG default flip earlier in this session.

Verification: syntax-checked (ast.parse), `verify.sh --no-server` green.
--- a/v1/kv_offload/transfer_log.py
+++ b/v1/kv_offload/transfer_log.py
