+time -- one tier below v1/engine/request_lifecycle_log.py's NEW REQUEST/
+FINISHED lines (one per request, on by default). Off by default; set
+VLLM_KV_TRANSFER_LOG=1 to watch it live.
+
+When enabled, this module emits one INFO line per transfer, interspersed
+in the normal log:
 
     KV LOAD  chatcmpl-a9b273614cd4c815 | fs   -> RAM  |  44 blk
     KV LOAD  chatcmpl-a9b273614cd4c815 | RAM  -> VRAM |  44 blk /  36608 tok (had 50752 tok, now 87360 tok in VRAM)
@@ -45,10 +51,15 @@
 ``fs -> RAM`` then ``RAM -> VRAM``, which is the staged promotion the tiering
 manager actually performs (secondary tiers cannot touch GPU memory directly).
 
-Set VLLM_KV_TRANSFER_LOG=0 to silence it (this silences EVICT lines too).
-It is deliberately INFO and on by default: the whole point is to be
-visible next to the request log without turning on DEBUG for all of
-vLLM, which buries it.
+Set VLLM_KV_TRANSFER_LOG=1 to turn it on (silences to off again with 0 or
+by leaving it unset). Deliberately INFO rather than DEBUG so it's cheap to
+flip on next to the request log without turning on DEBUG for all of vLLM
+(which buries it) -- but off by default: at typical request rates this is
+several lines per request (one per chunk, per tier hop, plus batched
+EVICT lines), which is too much for routine watching. NEW REQUEST/
+FINISHED (v1/engine/request_lifecycle_log.py, on by default) is the
+per-request summary; turn this on when you need the per-transfer detail
+behind it.
 """
 
